          "sides": [
            {
              "id": 2315,
              "content": "Five characteristic skin findings that may be present in dermatomyositis"
            },
            {
              "id": 2316,
              "content": "<div>1. Gottron papules (scaly, purplish papules and plaques on the extensor surfaces of the metacarpophalangeal and interphalangeal joints)</div><div>2. Mechanic's hands (rough, cracked, dirty-appearing skin on the lateral surfaces and tips of the fingers)</div><div>3. Heliotrope rash (dusky purple discoloration of the upper eyelids and periorbital tissues)</div><div>4. V-Sign (erythematous rash in a V shape over the lower neck and upper chest)</div><div>5. Shawl sign (erythematous rash over the upper back, back of the neck, and shoulders)</div>"
            }
          ]
